{"availability":"available","full":"OneRedPanda99/sc-alpr-radar","name":"sc-alpr-radar","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-18T18:22:49Z","updated":"2026-10-10T14:49:02Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://oneredpanda99.github.io/sc-alpr-radar/**","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:09.706Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:09.706Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:09.706Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T15:06:09.706Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Personal, offline-first phone PWA for South Carolina. Maps ALPR / plate-reader cameras (Flock and other brands), live SCDOT traffic cameras, and city/police CCTV, warns you like a radar detector as you approach them, draws field-of-view cones, and plans camera-avoidance routes with turn-by-turn directions.","Awareness tool only. Does not alter, obscure, jam, or interfere with any camera or your license plate. Keep your plate legible and drive attentively.","A naive %flock% search is almost all noise — restaurants, home networks, sports puns. Validating against known OSM ALPR positions showed the exact SSID Flock lands within 200 m of a mapped ALPR 38% of the time, against a 2.1% control rate for random nearby points — roughly an 18x enrichment. Broader patterns did not survive that test. Re-run the validation before adding a signature."],"features":["Drive mode — follow-me map, FOV cones, category-colored markers, rich","proximity card (name, brand/type, facing, purpose, live photo), radar beep, wake lock. Bottom-left chips toggle Plate / Traffic layers, Map/Satellite, and + Add camera.","Route mode — origin + destination, fastest vs avoid-cameras (avoidance","weighs plate readers only), highlighted route line, turn-by-turn list, save into Drive.","Add your own cameras — tap + Add camera, pick plate vs t